<!DOCTYPE qhelp PUBLIC
  "-//Semmle//qhelp//EN"
  "qhelp.dtd">
<qhelp>
<overview>
<p>
A derivation overrides <code>patchPhase</code> or <code>fixupPhase</code>
directly. Those phases in <code>stdenv</code> do important default work that
many nixpkgs packages rely on.
</p>
<p>
<code>patchPhase</code> applies entries from <code>patches</code>.
<code>fixupPhase</code> runs post-install fixups such as stripping binaries and
applying ELF / RPATH fixups through setup hooks. Replacing either phase
wholesale can silently drop that behaviour unless it is reimplemented by hand.
</p>
</overview>

<recommendation>
<p>
Keep the default phase and extend it with <code>prePatch</code> /
<code>postPatch</code> or <code>preFixup</code> / <code>postFixup</code>
instead. If the goal is to disable one fixup action, prefer the targeted knob
for that action (for example <code>dontStrip</code> or
<code>dontPatchELF</code>) rather than replacing all of
<code>fixupPhase</code>.
</p>
</recommendation>

<example>
<p>Problematic — overrides <code>fixupPhase</code> directly:</p>
<sample language="nix">
{ stdenv }:
stdenv.mkDerivation {
  pname = "demo";
  version = "1.0";
  fixupPhase = ''
    echo "custom fixup"
  '';
}
</sample>
<p>Recommended — keep the default phase and extend it with a hook:</p>
<sample language="nix">
{ stdenv }:
stdenv.mkDerivation {
  pname = "demo";
  version = "1.0";
  postFixup = ''
    echo "custom fixup"
  '';
}
</sample>
<p>The same pattern applies to <code>patchPhase</code>: prefer
<code>prePatch</code> / <code>postPatch</code> to replacing the phase.</p>
</example>

<references>
<li>
<a href="https://github.com/jtojnar/nixpkgs-hammering/blob/main/explanations/fixup-phase.md">
<code>nixpkgs-hammering</code> explanation: <code>fixup-phase</code></a>
</li>
<li>
<a href="https://github.com/jtojnar/nixpkgs-hammering/blob/main/explanations/patch-phase.md">
<code>nixpkgs-hammering</code> explanation: <code>patch-phase</code></a>
</li>
</references>
</qhelp>
